WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.803 --> 00:00:06.838
Priya Raman: Hi Megan, how's it going?

2
00:00:07.365 --> 00:00:17.330
Megan Foster: Hey Priya, pretty good. Busy week. We had two practices short-staffed, so so I'm covering front desk at the Meridian location this afternoon.

3
00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:18.630
Megan Foster: How about you?

4
00:00:19.382 --> 00:00:26.635
Priya Raman: Oh, hanging in there. Lots of Q4 planning on my side. Thanks for making time. I know afternoons are hectic.

5
00:00:27.105 --> 00:00:32.657
Megan Foster: Yeah, no problem. Let me just close my office door so I can actually hear you.

6
00:00:34.044 --> 00:00:47.606
Priya Raman: Okay. So I I pulled your account before we hopped on. Call volume looks steady. You're around 3,400 calls last month across the 19 practices, which is up a bit from August.

7
00:00:48.603 --> 00:00:58.624
Megan Foster: Yeah, that tracks. September is always a little bumpy with school schedules. A lot of new-patient calls, which is what we care about.

8
00:00:58.869 --> 00:01:06.092
Priya Raman: Right. And I saw the Signal AI setup is classifying new patient versus existing patient pretty cleanly. Anything there feel off?

9
00:01:07.516 --> 00:01:14.353
Megan Foster: No, that part's fine. The practice managers read the call summaries every morning, that's just part of their routine now.

10
00:01:15.068 --> 00:01:21.428
Priya Raman: Good. And how's the Google Ads side looking? I know that's the piece tied to your new-patient budget.

11
00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:35.980
Megan Foster: Um, so that's actually the thing I wanted to bring up. The offline conversions do make it into Google Ads, they show up, but they're landing one to three days after the call. Sometimes longer if it's a weekend.

12
00:01:36.686 --> 00:01:39.638
Priya Raman: Okay, so the conversions arrive, just not same day.

13
00:01:40.365 --> 00:01:54.545
Megan Foster: Right. And the problem is Smart Bidding is looking at that data while it's still incomplete. If I've got 40 new-patient calls on a Monday and only 12 conversions have posted by Tuesday morning, the algorithm thinks Monday was a bad day.

14
00:01:54.545 --> 00:01:56.233
Megan Foster: Uh, so it pulls back.

15
00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:02.924
Priya Raman: And then the rest of the week's budget gets set off that picture.

16
00:02:03.685 --> 00:02:15.141
Megan Foster: Exactly. I can't make daily budget calls. I've basically stopped adjusting bids intraday because I don't trust what I'm seeing. Uh, I just let it run and hope the weekly view evens out.

17
00:02:16.338 --> 00:02:21.097
Priya Raman: Got it. How long has it been like this, do you think?

18
00:02:21.791 --> 00:02:31.301
Megan Foster: I noticed it uh, maybe... six weeks ago? End of August. I kept thinking it was a reporting delay on Google's side, but it's consistent.

19
00:02:32.761 --> 00:02:35.780
Priya Raman: Okay. And is it all campaigns, or certain ones?

20
00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:44.428
Megan Foster: As far as I can tell it's all of them. We run separate campaigns by service line, implants, general, ortho referrals.

21
00:02:44.428 --> 00:02:45.550
Megan Foster: They all lag.

22
00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:58.717
Priya Raman: Got it. I don't want to guess at what's happening there. Let me take this back I mean, to our team and see what's going on with the timing.

23
00:02:58.717 --> 00:03:08.577
Priya Raman: Can you send me a couple of call examples, dates and the GCLID if you have it? I know that's a pain to pull.

24
00:03:09.148 --> 00:03:14.623
Megan Foster: Uh, yeah, I can grab a few from last week. I'll email them over tomorrow morning.

25
00:03:15.879 --> 00:03:25.955
Priya Raman: Perfect. And if it helps, note which campaign and the day the conversion showed up versus the call date. That'll give the team something concrete.

26
00:03:27.218 --> 00:03:31.746
Megan Foster: Will do. Honestly I mostly wanted to make sure I wasn't imagining it.

27
00:03:33.011 --> 00:03:37.922
Priya Raman: No, that's a real thing to flag. Thanks for walking me through it.

28
00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:42.466
Megan Foster: Sure. Sorry, one sec, my front desk line is blowing up.

29
00:03:43.582 --> 00:03:44.623
Priya Raman: Take your time.

30
00:03:45.227 --> 00:03:46.880
Megan Foster: Okay, sorry. Where were we?

31
00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:53.703
Priya Raman: The uh, conversion timing. I've got it. Anything else on the Meta side while we're here?

32
00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:58.447
Megan Foster: Meta's fine. We're not spending much there right now anyway.

33
00:03:58.795 --> 00:04:10.081
Priya Raman: Okay. Let me look at a couple of other things. Your tracking numbers, are they all still mapped right? Any new locations since we last talked?

34
00:04:11.436 --> 00:04:20.380
Megan Foster: No new locations. We're still at 19. Though we're opening a satellite in Nampa in the spring, but that's a 2027 thing.

35
00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:27.871
Priya Raman: Um, Good to know. We can plan for that closer to the time. And seats, you're at 22, still accurate?

36
00:04:29.198 --> 00:04:37.941
Megan Foster: Yeah. We added a marketing coordinator in July, that's the 22nd. She's mostly doing content, but but she pokes around in the call data sometimes.

37
00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:42.553
Priya Raman: Um, okay. I'll keep that in mind for anything I send over.

38
00:04:43.199 --> 00:04:52.731
Megan Foster: Sounds good. Oh, and before I forget, can we move our next check-in? I've got a board thing the first week of November.

39
00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.748
Priya Raman: Yeah, of course. What about the the second week?

40
00:04:58.208 --> 00:05:01.096
Megan Foster: Like, Second week works. Tuesday or Wednesday.

41
00:05:02.313 --> 00:05:06.424
Priya Raman: I'll send an invite for Wednesday the 11th, same time.

42
00:05:07.025 --> 00:05:07.825
Megan Foster: Perfect.

43
00:05:08.631 --> 00:05:15.692
Priya Raman: So I'll chase the conversion timing with the team, and you'll send the examples. Anything else that's top of mind?

44
00:05:17.181 --> 00:05:24.734
Megan Foster: No, that's the big one. Everything else is running. I've got to get back out there, the waiting room is filling up.

45
00:05:25.764 --> 00:05:28.842
Priya Raman: Go, go. Thanks Megan. Um, Talk soon.

46
00:05:30.221 --> 00:05:31.903
Megan Foster: Thanks Priya. Uh, Bye.
